WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.310 --> 00:00:01.770
Nine forty-one.

2
00:00:01.770 --> 00:00:03.210
Checkout slows.

3
00:00:03.210 --> 00:00:04.510
Orders start to fail.

4
00:00:04.510 --> 00:00:06.110
So the hunt begins.

5
00:00:06.110 --> 00:00:07.010
Metrics.

6
00:00:07.010 --> 00:00:07.990
Kubernetes.

7
00:00:07.990 --> 00:00:09.130
The database.

8
00:00:09.130 --> 00:00:09.930
Logs.

9
00:00:09.930 --> 00:00:10.870
Deploys.

10
00:00:10.870 --> 00:00:12.090
The status page.

11
00:00:12.090 --> 00:00:12.860
The wiki.

12
00:00:12.860 --> 00:00:14.040
One engineer.

13
00:00:14.040 --> 00:00:15.080
Seven tools.

14
00:00:15.430 --> 00:00:16.970
The hour goes to looking,

15
00:00:16.970 --> 00:00:17.970
not deciding.

16
00:00:19.520 --> 00:00:21.510
Now give that ticket to one agent.

17
00:00:21.510 --> 00:00:22.890
It connects the signals.

18
00:00:22.890 --> 00:00:24.490
The payment provider slowed.

19
00:00:24.490 --> 00:00:25.570
Not your deploy.

20
00:00:25.760 --> 00:00:28.320
It picks a runbook your team already tested.

21
00:00:28.460 --> 00:00:30.060
Then it asks a person,

22
00:00:30.060 --> 00:00:31.940
with the evidence and an undo,

23
00:00:31.940 --> 00:00:34.019
in the ticket, Slack or Teams.

24
00:00:34.330 --> 00:00:36.690
Nothing runs until someone says yes.

25
00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:39.560
It runs the fix, checks checkout recovered,

26
00:00:39.560 --> 00:00:41.160
and logs every step.

27
00:00:41.260 --> 00:00:43.360
Risk decides what runs on its own.

28
00:00:43.360 --> 00:00:44.400
Not the AI.

29
00:00:44.610 --> 00:00:46.810
You start on recommendations only.

30
00:00:46.810 --> 00:00:48.330
We baseline thirty days,

31
00:00:48.330 --> 00:00:49.870
then report every month.

32
00:00:50.110 --> 00:00:52.270
Crozaint builds it on the tools you already

33
00:00:52.270 --> 00:00:52.830
run.

34
00:00:53.260 --> 00:00:54.980
The agent does the legwork.

35
00:00:54.980 --> 00:00:56.660
Your engineer makes the call.
